TTL (Time To Live)

TTL determines how long DNS responses remain cached.

Example:

TTL = 300 seconds

DNS servers reuse the cached answer for 5 minutes before checking again.

Lower TTL:

Faster updates
More DNS queries

Higher TTL:

Better performance
More caching
